Experimental repository to provide glue for seamlessly integrating cargo build
with flutter plugins and packages.

See https://matejknopp.com/post/flutter_plugin_in_rust_with_no_prebuilt_binaries/
for a tutorial on how to use Cargokit.

Example plugin available at https://github.com/irondash/hello_rust_ffi_plugin.

For Android plugins that need the NDK's shared C++ runtime, enable copying it in
the plugin's Gradle configuration:

```groovy
cargokit {
    manifestDir = "../rust"
    libname = "my_crate"
    copyLibcxxShared = true
}
```

`copyLibcxxShared` defaults to `false`. When enabled, Cargokit copies the
matching NDK `libc++_shared.so` beside the Rust libraries for each Android ABI.

